  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in feet per minute, we divide the number of feet, $602,$ by the number of minutes, $4.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{602}{4} & =\\frac{602\u00f72}{4\u00f72} \\\\  & =\\frac{301}{2} \\\\  & =301\u00f72 \\\\  & =150.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the elevator is $150.5$ feet per minute.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
